{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issues_index.json\\\")); nums={2890,3115,175,157,2738}; [print(\\\"\\\\n---\\\",x[\\\"number\\\"],x[\\\"title\\\"],\\\"---\\\\n\\\",x.get(\\\"body\\\",\\\"\\\")) for x in d if x[\\\"number\\\"] in nums]'\"","aggregated_output":"\n--- 157 Issues with table wrapping ---\n Not sure if it is a bug or expected behavior for version 3.3.0 and fact that ratio/flexible feature is undocumented is not helping.\r\n\r\nI have table with three columns. All three using default settings + `no_wrap=True` as I want them always to occupy a single line.\r\nThere is scenario where column B is so wide that even with overflow column A have width 0 and it barely reacting to `width` argument.\r\n\r\nThis is my dream configuration. It is even achievable with this library?\r\nColumn A - No wrap. No overflow. Always display entire content.\r\nColumn B - No wrap. Overflow. Let it take most of the space.\r\nColumn C - No wrap. Overflow only if B is really, really wide.\n\n--- 175 [REQUEST] Column sorting for table ---\n Have you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\r\n\r\n**How would you improve Rich?**\r\n\r\nSort apis for table.\r\n\r\nEither as part of add column\r\ntable.add_column(sort=\"asc\")\r\n\r\nOr once the table is fully loaded\r\ntable.add_sort(column name/column index/column ref, asc/desc, comparator=default comparator)\r\n\r\n**What problem does it solved for you?**\r\n\r\nSorting is an important part of a table.\r\n\r\nWhat problem do you have that this feature would solve? I may be able to suggest an existing way of solving it.\r\nMy product [scan](https://github.com/ShiftLeftSecurity/sast-scan) can display results sorted by multiple columns.\r\n\n\n--- 2738 [BUG] \"collapse_padding=True\" setting doesn't work for first table column ---\n ```\r\nfrom rich.console import Console\r\nfrom rich.table import Table\r\n\r\nconsole = Console()\r\n\r\ntable = Table(title=\"Star Wars Movies\", collapse_padding=True)\r\n\r\ntable.add_column(\"Test1\", style=\"green\")\r\ntable.add_column(\"Test2\", style=\"magenta\")\r\ntable.add_row(\"Dec 20, 2019\", \"Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker\", \"$952,110,690\")\r\nconsole.print(table)\r\n```\r\n\r\n![1 cleaned](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/61022210/211255212-1cfdf1a4-1061-4016-8afb-5ddebd7e9696.png)\r\nPay attention to the first column. All columns are left aligned except for the first column\r\n\r\n\"**collapse_padding=True**\" is responsible for this\r\nPerhaps this is not a bug, but it is intended for the first column.\r\n\r\nLinux deb; python3.10; rich v13.0.1\n\n--- 2890 [BUG] table column no_wrap can squash columns below their min_width ---\n - [X] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions.\r\n- [X] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md).\r\n\r\n**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nI'll start with:  the bug may be with my understanding of options, so I'm prepared to accept that I'm thinking about things wrong.  That said, I feel pretty confident that my thinking is not incoherent. 😉\r\n\r\nIn a table column, the no_wrap option does not function as I would expect.  My expectation is that the content of a column would not be allowed to wrap, and that the overflow property would apply.  Further, that with no specification of the column's width, its width would be determined by finding the total available table width, meeting the width requirements of other columns (and borders) and then using the remaining space.\r\n\r\nInstead, a no_wrap column is forcing other table column contents to be squashed below their minimum width.  Consider this program:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom rich import print\r\nfrom rich.table import Table\r\nfrom rich.text import Text\r\n\r\ntable = Table(show_header=True, header_style=\"bold magenta\")\r\ntable.add_column(\"Issue\", min_width=7, width=7)\r\ntable.add_column(\"S\", min_width=1, width=1)\r\ntable.add_column(\"Pri\", min_width=3, width=3)\r\ntable.add_column(\"Title\", overflow=\"ellipsis\")\r\n\r\ntoo_long = \"\"\"\\\r\nThis is a full line sentence and it fills a whole line so it overflows a cell!\\\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nfor i in range(2):\r\n    table.add_row(\"ABC-123\", \"X\", \"123\", \" \".join([too_long, too_long]))\r\n\r\nprint(table)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis prints the following table on my 80 column terminal (iTerm2):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"881\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-03-21 at 20 05 58\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30682/226768923-a78b56c2-a3c7-4a09-a69e-e9b3b68accaf.png\">\r\n\r\nIf I update the program to use no_wrap:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom rich import print\r\nfrom rich.table import\n\n--- 3115 [BUG] Rich markdown printed to console only shows a single link in a column/ table cell ---\n - [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions.\r\n- [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md).\r\n\r\n**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nI use Rich to format a pandas data frame with multiple links in some column to markdown and show it in the terminal. However, when there are more than a single link in a column rich only shows the last one?\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom rich.console import Console\r\nfrom rich.markdown import Markdown\r\n\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\nmd_table = pd.DataFrame(\r\n    {\r\n        \"links\": [\"[page1](https://www.example.com/page1), [page2](https://www.example.com/page2)\"]\r\n    }\r\n).to_markdown()\r\n\r\nconsole = Console()\r\nconsole.print(Markdown(md_table))\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n```bash\r\n      links  \r\n ━━━━━━━━━━━ \r\n  0   page2  \r\n```\r\n\r\nExpected\r\n```\r\n      links  \r\n ━━━━━━━━━━━ \r\n  0   page1, page2  \r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I write the markdown to a file I get the expected table with multiple links...\r\n\r\n**Platform**\r\n\r\nplatform=\"Darwin\"\r\nrich==13.5.2\r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
